!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-family-through-a-template.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/40/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A family whose members compose an application and pin the selector there ([TSON-SCHEMA] §5.2, §5.8, §5.10). A
  template is not a type, so a family is declared with records, and an application's IS-A edges are its template's
  written parents'.

  `pet` is the base: an abstract record stating the selector and the field every member shares. `pet_of` composes it,
  and each member composes an application of `pet_of` and pins `kind`. `dog` reaches `pet` through `pet_of`'s written
  parent, never through `pet_of` itself, so a position typed `pet` dispatches over `dog` and `cat` by the selector.

  `tpet` is an abstract template, and `abstract` on a template is each application's `extension`: `tpet<text>` is an
  abstract record with the selector `kind`, an abstract base in its own right. `tdog` and `tcat` compose that application
  and pin `kind`, so each IS-A the entry `tpet<text>` denotes, and a position typed `tpet<text>` dispatches over them.
  """
!schema {
  dog_type => { breed: text }
  cat_type => { indoor: boolean }

  pet    => abstract { kind: text =?  name: text }
  pet_of => <T> pet & { pet: T }
  dog    => pet_of<dog_type> & { kind?: = "dog" }
  cat    => pet_of<cat_type> & { kind?: = "cat" }

  tpet => abstract <B> { kind: text =?  name: text  extra?: B }
  tdog => tpet<text> & { kind?: = "dog"  breed: text }
  tcat => tpet<text> & { kind?: = "cat"  indoor: boolean }

  holder => {
    p: pet
    t?: tpet<text>?
  }
}
